  "summary_en": "The Planar Inflate node turns a 2D signed distance field into a smooth height layer, inflating the region inside the shape boundary. Optional wrinkle and mound noise breaks up the surface for base terrain, cushion-like shapes or texture displacement.",
  "inputs": [
    "sdf: layer holding the signed distance field to inflate"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Height Scale: multiplies the base inflation; negative values invert it",
    "Pre Scale: base inflation strength before the height is solved",
    "Noise Scale: amount of Wrinkles and Mounds noise added",
    "Wrinkles: fine phasor noise (Size, Boundary Blend, Seed)",
    "Mounds: broader fractal noise (Size, Max Octaves, Lacunarity, Roughness)",
    "Blur: smooths the noise and blends it with the shape (Scale, Mask from Boundary, Mask Smoothing)",
    "Iterations: Poisson solve iterations; more gives a more converged result but is slower"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Inflating directly at the image edge can produce artifacts; SideFX suggests adjusting the SDF radius so it stays inside the image boundary.",
    "If the height has flat areas, increase Iterations."
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Planar Inflate gonfle une distance signée 2D en hauteur lisse, avec des rides et des monticules de bruit optionnels."
}
